॰ ---------------------------------------------------------------- Windows: the PE32+ image
॰ pe() in anuvada.py: the headers in the first page, .text (code, table, image) at RVA 0x1000,
॰ .data (the kernel32 import tables, then the frame as zero fill), and on arm64 a .reloc
॰ holding one empty block. FileAlignment = SectionAlignment = 4 KiB, so a file offset is its
॰ RVA. TimeDateStamp and CheckSum are 0: the output is a function of the input.

॰ the header fields and the import tables (pehdr.py, checked against the oracle); the
॰ वातायन… globals carry the values
